   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the state law, in relation to assembly and senate districts",
    "basePrintNo": "S8197",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8197-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§121 & 127, State L (as proposed in S.8185-A & A.9040-A)",
    "lawSection": "State Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8197\n\nSPONSOR: GIANARIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the state law, in relation to assembly and senate\ndistricts\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to make technical corrections to a chapter\nof the laws of 2022 amending the State Law in relation to establishing\nAssembly and Senate districts, as proposed in legislative bills numbers\nS.8185-A and A.9040-A, in order to effectuate the intent of the law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill would make technical corrections to Article 8 of the State\nLaw, as amended by a chapter of the laws of 2022, in order to provide\nCounty, County Subdivisions, Census Tract, and Census Block descriptions\nof 150 Assembly districts and 63 Senate districts.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill establishes new legislative districts for the state Senate and\nAssembly. It is based on population figures from the 2020 Federal Census\nand population figures calculated in accordance with the Prisoner Allo-\ncation Law of 2010 (N.Y. Con. L. § 71(8)1 N.Y. Leg. L. § 83-M). The\ndistricts comply with the United States and New York State Constitutions\nand the requirements of the Federal Voting Rights Act.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill would take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2022 amending the State Law relating to estab-\nlishing Assembly and Senate districts, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.8185-A and A.9040-A, takes effect.\n",
